        documentation: {
          purpose: "A binary form input for toggling a boolean value. Supports checked, unchecked, and indeterminate states. Use in forms where multiple independent options can be selected.",
          usage: "Always pair with a Label component for accessibility \u2014 connect them via matching id and htmlFor props, or use aria-labelledby. onChange receives the click event, not the new checked state (there is no onCheckedChange): to read or react to the state, control it with value plus your own state, e.g. const [checked, setChecked] = useState<boolean | 'indeterminate'>(false) and onChange={() => setChecked((previous) => previous !== true)}. Use defaultValue for uncontrolled usage when the state isn't needed. Use value='indeterminate' for partial selection states (e.g. select-all with mixed children). Use RadioList when only one option from a group can be selected. Use Switch for binary settings that take immediate effect rather than form submission.",
          properties: "size: large\nemphasis: weak\nvalue: unchecked, checked, indeterminate\nstatus: default, error\nstate: default, hover, active, focus, disabled",
          related: [
            "RadioList",
            "Switch"
          ],
          origin: "released-metadata",
          metadataSource: "packages/components/src/components/Checkbox/Checkbox.metadata.json",
          links: [
            {
              uri: "https://github.com/Frontify/fondue/tree/ebcc9b8579a7f862f43a2732f5a5b9c3105e6796/packages/components/src/components/Checkbox/Checkbox.metadata.json"
            },
            {
              uri: "https://fondue.frontify.com/"
            }
          ],
          description: "A binary form input for toggling a boolean value. Supports checked, unchecked, and indeterminate states. Use in forms where multiple independent options can be selected.\n\nAlways pair with a Label component for accessibility \u2014 connect them via matching id and htmlFor props, or use aria-labelledby. onChange receives the click event, not the new checked state (there is no onCheckedChange): to read or react to the state, control it with value plus your own state, e.g. const [checked, setChecked] = useState<boolean | 'indeterminate'>(false) and onChange={() => setChecked((previous) => previous !== true)}. Use defaultValue for uncontrolled usage when the state isn't needed. Use value='indeterminate' for partial selection states (e.g. select-all with mixed children). Use RadioList when only one option from a group can be selected. Use Switch for binary settings that take immediate effect rather than form submission.\n\nExposed variant properties:\nsize: large\nemphasis: weak\nvalue: unchecked, checked, indeterminate\nstatus: default, error\nstate: default, hover, active, focus, disabled\n\nText properties edit the exposed content. Icon properties swap the native icon; Show properties control its visibility.\n\nCoverage: supported. Read-only shares default appearance and blocks interaction in code; error state keeps the source red border.\n\nSource: https://github.com/Frontify/fondue/tree/ebcc9b8579a7f862f43a2732f5a5b9c3105e6796/packages/components/src/components/Checkbox/Checkbox.metadata.json"
        }
