        documentation: {
          purpose: "A date or date range picker with a calendar panel. Use when the user needs to select a specific date or date range.",
          usage: "DatePicker does not include its own trigger or popover \u2014 combine DatePicker.Input as the Flyout.Trigger and DatePicker (or DatePicker.Range) inside Flyout.Content for the standard pattern. Dates are represented as plain objects { year, month, day } \u2014 not JS Date objects. Use DatePicker.Range for range selection. Pass disabledDates to grey out individual days. Pass minMonth and/or maxMonth to bound month navigation \u2014 the previous/next-month controls disable once the bound month is reached.",
          properties: "selected: , 2026-10-20..2026-10-24",
          related: [
            "TextInput"
          ],
          origin: "released-metadata",
          metadataSource: "packages/components/src/components/DatePicker/DatePicker.metadata.json",
          links: [
            {
              uri: "https://github.com/Frontify/fondue/tree/ebcc9b8579a7f862f43a2732f5a5b9c3105e6796/packages/components/src/components/DatePicker/DatePicker.ts"
            },
            {
              uri: "https://fondue.frontify.com/"
            }
          ],
          description: "A date or date range picker with a calendar panel. Use when the user needs to select a specific date or date range.\n\nDatePicker does not include its own trigger or popover \u2014 combine DatePicker.Input as the Flyout.Trigger and DatePicker (or DatePicker.Range) inside Flyout.Content for the standard pattern. Dates are represented as plain objects { year, month, day } \u2014 not JS Date objects. Use DatePicker.Range for range selection. Pass disabledDates to grey out individual days. Pass minMonth and/or maxMonth to bound month navigation \u2014 the previous/next-month controls disable once the bound month is reached.\n\nExposed variant properties:\nselected: , 2026-10-20..2026-10-24\n\nText properties edit the exposed content. Icon properties swap the native icon; Show properties control its visibility.\n\nCoverage: partial. selected is serialized sample range notation for design only; runtime API takes a DatePickerDateRange. Source joined middle/start/end per-corner radii are not fully reproduced by the current symmetric radius schema. Native static definitions do not implement browser event handlers, focus management or accessibility semantics. Source styling and finite states are encoded here; visual parity still requires Figma runtime review.\n\nSource: https://github.com/Frontify/fondue/tree/ebcc9b8579a7f862f43a2732f5a5b9c3105e6796/packages/components/src/components/DatePicker/DatePicker.ts"
        }
