          description: "A hover-triggered hint overlay that provides additional context for an element. Use for icon-only buttons, truncated text, or any UI element that benefits from a brief explanation.\n\nCompose as Tooltip.Root > Tooltip.Trigger + Tooltip.Content. Use asChild on Tooltip.Trigger to forward tooltip behavior onto a custom element (e.g. a Button). Default enter delay is 700ms \u2014 use enterDelay=0 for immediate display. Tooltip.Content appears on hover; use Flyout for click-triggered contextual panels with richer content.\n\nExposed variant properties:\npadding: compact, spacious\nside: top, right, bottom, left\n\nText properties edit the exposed content. Icon properties swap the native icon; Show properties control its visibility.\n\nCoverage: partial. Content-only set; Root delay/open state and viewport collision do not affect intrinsic appearance. Arrow drop-shadow outline and maxWidth/custom children wrapping need native visual QA. Native static definitions do not implement browser event handlers, focus management or accessibility semantics. Source styling and finite states are encoded here; visual parity still requires Figma runtime review.\n\nSource: https://github.com/Frontify/fondue/tree/ebcc9b8579a7f862f43a2732f5a5b9c3105e6796/packages/components/src/components/Tooltip/Tooltip.tsx"
